# Opinions with a reason: fun, boring, easy, hard and more, joined with because.
lesson language-because v=1 format=teach grade=4 unit=8 subject=language levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Opinions and [[opinion.because]]"
  goal "Give an opinion in [[language.name]] with a reason."

  look {
    scene 24x14 {
      column all at=canvas(1, 1) space=1 align=start {
        comic why who=["girl", "boy"] says=["[[opinion.do-you-like-football]]", "[[opinion.yes-i-like-it-because-it-is-fun]]"] moods=["happy", "excited"] with=["", ""] thinks=[0, 0] holds=["", "ball"] labels=["1", "2"]
      }
    }
    say """
      To give a reason, join it with [[opinion.because]], because:
      [[phrase.i-like-football-because-it-is-fun]], I like football because it is fun. Other
      reasons: [[opinion.boring]] (boring), [[opinion.easy]] (easy), [[opinion.hard]] (hard),
      [[opinion.interesting]] (interesting), [[opinion.great]] (great). [[phrase.why]] asks why.
      [[phrase.i-love-swimming]] means I love swimming, and [[phrase.i-hate-the-rain]] means I hate
      the rain.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked language.because-name k=3
    }
    show language.because-name k=2 easy-k=0 hard-k=4
    show language.because-meaning k=3 easy-k=1 hard-k=4
    show language.because-write k=3 easy-k=2 hard-k=5
    show language.because-name k=4 easy-k=1 hard-k=5
    show language.because-match k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    show language.because-write k=4
    show language.because-listen k=3 easy-k=0 hard-k=5
    show language.because-say k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    level hard {
      show language.because-write k=3
    }
  }
  language es {
    try stars=2 {
      show language.es-because-why k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
    }
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show language.because-puzzle k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
  }
  remember {
    say "An opinion and a reason, joined: [[phrase.i-like-football-because-it-is-fun]]"
  }

  grown-ups """
    The wrong idea to watch for is the word that asks why and the word that says because treated as
    one, which the two-star question asks about, and a reason that does not match the plural it
    describes. The naming questions put a situation in words and a face beside it; the face shows
    the feeling and the word names the reason. Loving is stronger than liking, and the three-star
    question asks the child to rank them. From this grade the written words are marked with their
    accents: a word typed without its accent is not taken. The dictation is read from this sheet,
    where it prints as Read aloud, or played by the device. If the child is stuck, ask why in
    English about something they like, then say the reason in the language together. Off the page,
    give three opinions a day in the language with a reason. It meets England's key stage 2
    languages programme (years 3 to 6, statutory from age 7): "engage in conversations; ask and
    answer questions; express opinions and respond to those of others"; Japan's grades 5 and 6
    foreign languages: "Can exchange their own thoughts and feelings regarding familiar and simple
    matters in daily life by using simple words and phrases and basic expressions"; and CEFR A2,
    "Can understand sentences and frequently used expressions related to areas of most immediate
    relevance". The phrases are in [[language.variety]].
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level [[opinion.hard]] is worked first in the teacher's pen, the words to name are [[opinion.fun]] and [[opinion.boring]] and the words to write are [[opinion.easy]] and [[opinion.great]], the plainer ones of the lesson, with the first set to match, the shortest sentence to hear and the first version of each star question."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the words to name are [[opinion.interesting]] and [[opinion.delicious]] and the words to write are [[opinion.because]], [[opinion.great]] and [[opinion.hard]], the ones most often mixed up, with the last set to match, the longest sentence to hear, a third word to write and the last version of each star question."
  }
}
